I wanted to be a cop.

254
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:35,009
Even as a kid, I dreamed of becoming
the most respectable officer I could be.

255
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:39,200
Back then, I also had the
kind of will you possess now.

256
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,880
However, I screwed up big time.

257
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:44,057
There's a word for folks like me.

258
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:45,493
We're utterly hopeless.

259
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,440
We never see things through to the end.

260
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:52,040
And our shortcomings
always lead to failure.

261
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:55,080
You couldn't be more wrong, Abakyo.

262
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:59,580
The path you're on is righteous and just.

263
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,320
Our will is the same.

264
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:06,308
That will you possessed when you were
only a fledgling police officer remains.

265
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:11,480
It still burns inside you as brightly
and dutifully as ever, Abbacchio.

266
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,297
But how…

267
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,740
how could you possibly know my name?

268
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,780
Hang on just a second.

269
00:16:19,160 --> 00:16:22,080
I have this feeling we've
met before, but where?

270
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:28,060
Where are you going, Abbacchio?

271
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:30,397
I'm getting on that bus.

272
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,197
It's all coming back to me now.

273
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:33,320
That's right.

274
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:34,897
I have to get out of here.

275
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:37,557
I have to help my comrades
with what's coming.

276
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,320
Have you forgotten, Abakyo?

277
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,240
You came here on that bus.

278
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,180
It's a last stop, I'm afraid.

279
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:46,920
There's no going back. Not ever.

280
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,900
Wait. It's you.

281
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:56,420
All along, it was you.

282
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:59,660
I took that damn bribe
and you paid the price.

283
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:04,280
Oh, Abakyo, you've done
so much good since then.

284
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:12,960
Hear me when I say, I am
so proud of you, amiko mio.

285
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:21,500
Oh god, no!

286
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:23,960
It's not real!

287
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:25,340
It's not!

288
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,720
It can't be!

289
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:28,677
You have to heal him, Giorno!

290
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:31,380
What are you waiting for? Fix this!

291
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:34,400
Do something before I kick your ass!

292
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:41,360
I'm sorry, but it was an
instant kill at close range.

293
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:42,977
We just didn't...

294
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:46,620
we didn't make it in time.

295
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,557
How could you do it, Ipaccio?

296
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,934
How could you let the enemy
get close enough to do this?

297
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,920
Mista, make sure Trish
stays in the turtle.

298
00:17:57,740 --> 00:18:01,564
It's highly likely our foe's next
move will be to come after her.

299
00:18:01,680 --> 00:18:02,960
We have to escape.

300
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,729
It's not safe for us here.

301
00:18:05,100 --> 00:18:06,680
This tragedy's my fault.

302
00:18:06,940 --> 00:18:08,637
We're getting out of this place.

303
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,367
Our investigation has ended.

304
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:13,240
What are you trying to
say here, Bucciarati?

305
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:15,817
Abacchio's gonna wake up any second!

306
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:16,730
Just you wait!

307
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:19,177
It'll take time, but he's coming back!

308
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:20,966
Give him a chance to wake up!

309
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,788
Tell him I'm right, Giorno!

310
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:24,862
Isn't that what happened before?

311
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:27,750
Hey, come on!

312
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:29,017
That is enough, Narancia!

313
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:30,865
We have to leave this instant.

314
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,471
Bring out Little Bomber and
start scouting an escape route.

315
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:37,032
What the hell are you saying, Bucciarati?

316
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:40,015
You're not making any sense right now!

317
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:43,597
They want to face the bastards
so I can blow their ass to bits!

318
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:46,357
If they're nearby, then they
need to come out and face me!

319
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:47,270
Right, Mista?

320
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:48,250
Did you know?

321
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:52,140
Hey, answer me, Mista!

322
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:55,480
Narancia, we have to go.

323
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:57,620
Listen to Bucciarati.

324
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:59,180
No, not you two.

325
00:18:59,900 --> 00:19:01,400
What is wrong with you?

326
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:03,248
Why are you being this way?

327
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:06,137
You've never been the guy to
turn your back on a comrade.

328
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:07,691
You bring him back to us.

329
00:19:07,840 --> 00:19:10,037
Do your friggin' job and start
growing some replacements.

330
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:11,238
This isn't helping.

331
00:19:11,420 --> 00:19:12,920
Narancia! I don't care!

332
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:25,700
Oh, fuck you.

333
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:33,222
So you're just leaving
him here to run, Pucinati?

334
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:38,257
After everything our group has been
through, how can you just walk away?

335
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:40,160
Don't ask me to abandon him.

336
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,920
Anything but that, please.

337
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:46,000
That is a direct order, Narancia.

338
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:49,246
Abakio was aware of the
risk and did his duty.

339
00:19:49,760 --> 00:19:50,660
We're leaving.

340
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:52,884
Wait, please, but you're at me!

341
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,090
What's that?

342
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,340
Bucciarati, don't go yet.

343
00:20:26,980 --> 00:20:29,392
Whatever this is, it must mean something.

344
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,500
It has to.

345
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:32,547
Yeah, but what's he holding?

346
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:33,780
I can't tell.

347
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:36,257
Right now, it looks like a normal rock.

348
00:20:36,340 --> 00:20:37,200
But I wonder.

349
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,312
Restore it, Golden Wind!

350
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:45,127
Return from whence you came.

351
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,880
Hey, take a look at this.

352
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:56,740
I think Abakio actually
managed to complete his replay.

353
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,140
This must be a death mask.

354
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:02,680
The replay created it.

355
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:05,800
Before Moody Jazz vanished, he succeeded.

356
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:10,220
He used the last of his stand
energy and imprinted this face here.

357
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:12,341
This pillar is like a lithograph.

358
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:15,880
Abakio, left behind the
message of a lifetime.

359
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:18,740
This is the visage of the boss!

360
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:24,360
Abakio, you've made everyone proud.

361
00:21:25,100 --> 00:21:29,200
Truly, your unrelenting
determination to uncover the truth

362
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:33,432
has made its way to the hearts
and minds of your comrades.

363
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:38,200
And that, my old friend,
is all that matters.

364
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:22,180
Stand up, join us Come on,

365
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:26,220
just say this a lie We are the power,

366
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:28,240
those days are future

367
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:34,220
Cause we are the fighters,
just fighting for a right

368
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:43,750
Thank you.

369
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,640
Thank you.
